From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:49:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 023/342] graphics: meson_hdmi driver and accelerant for the
 Amlogic GXBB

A native display driver for the Meson GXBB (S905, ODROID-C2) HDMI
output. U-Boot leaves the display pipeline running (power, clocks,
resets, HDMI controller and PHY setup) through ExitBootServices, so the
driver only reprograms what depends on the mode: the OSD1 canvas and
window, the VPP postblend width, the ENCP timing generator, the HDMI
PLL's OD2 post-divider (U-Boot's 5940 MHz VCO: /2 for 74.25 MHz, /1 for
148.5 MHz), the DesignWare frame composer (with a TMDS soft reset) and a
PHY reset.

At attach it compares U-Boot's live registers with the values computed
for its mode (all match for 1280x720), reads the EDID over the
controller's DDC master (two identical reads required), saves the boot
state, and allocates a contiguous write-combining frame buffer for
1920x1080. Modes: 1280x720@60, 1920x1080@30 and @60, as far as the EDID
lists them (detailed timings or CTA video codes); 1080p60 is preferred.
A failed mode set restores the boot mode; so does "meson_hdmi restore"
in KDL. "mode_setting off" in the driver settings leaves the device
unpublished, so app_server keeps the framebuffer driver.

The accelerant passes mode requests to the driver and exposes its mode
list, preferred mode and EDID.

Tested on the ODROID-C2 with an HDMI capture device: the desktop comes up
at 1920x1080@60; 720p60 and 1080p30 work; 10 switches between 720p and
1080p without a fault; the KDL restore brings back U-Boot's picture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
